{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Six days.</b> It juxtaposed this here on account of 'that the son of your maidservant and the stranger may be refreshed' — for he is poor and your hired laborer." "<b>And on the seventh day you shall rest.</b> Since the sabbatical year is called Shabbat, one might say there is no need to observe another Shabbat; therefore it teaches: <b>and on the seventh day you shall rest.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "סד״א = שמא דבר אמרתי expanded as 'one might say'; קמ״ל = קא משמע לן, 'therefore it teaches.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:01.836273227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}